{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts is designed so ordinary chart code names its application types\nonce. Data, channel outputs, scale domains, focus points, and framework props\nthen infer from the definition."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"infer-from-mark-channels","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Infer from mark channels"}]},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- docs-example: typescript-inference typecheck -->"},{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleTime } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\ninterface Reading {\n  id: string\n  recordedAt: Date\n  temperature: number\n}\n\nconst readings: readonly Reading[] = []\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(readings, {\n      x: 'recordedAt',\n      y: 'temperature',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleTime },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here the datum is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Reading"},{"type":"text","value":", x values are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Date"},{"type":"text","value":", and y values are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"},{"type":"text","value":".\nAn incompatible scale or channel field fails at the definition instead of\nsurfacing later in a tooltip callback."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"capture-application-values","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capture application values"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createTrafficDefinition(rows: readonly Reading[]) {\n  return defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      lineY(rows, {\n        x: 'recordedAt',\n        y: 'temperature',\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleTime },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework components should memoize the complete definition:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = useMemo(() => createTrafficDefinition(readings), [readings])\n\nreturn <Chart definition={definition} ariaLabel=\"Temperature history\" />","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition identity tells the host when captured application data or options\nchanged. A responsive definition callback still rebuilds when the host size\nchanges:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createTrafficDefinition(rows: readonly Reading[]) {\n  return defineChart(({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [\n      lineY(rows, {\n        x: 'recordedAt',\n        y: 'temperature',\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleTime },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n    },\n\n    margin: width < 480 ? 24 : 40,\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-literal-information","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep literal information"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"field-name channels such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x: 'recordedAt'"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typed accessors when a value is derived;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChart({...})"},{"type":"text","value":" or a responsive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChart(() => ({...}))"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"satisfies"},{"type":"text","value":" when naming a configuration object separately."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Avoid annotating an intermediate object as broad "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpec"},{"type":"text","value":" before passing it\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChart"},{"type":"text","value":". That discards the literal mark tuple used for axis and\ncallback inference."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mark tuple determines the value type accepted by each reserved positional\nscale. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.x"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.y"},{"type":"text","value":" are always present in canonical definitions.\nUse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" for a dimension that no mark materializes. Named scale selectors on\nmarks keep those values out of the reserved entry's inferred type."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"callback-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and selection callbacks receive the original datum and inferred\ncoordinate types:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Temperature readings\"\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (!point) return\n    point.datum.recordedAt // Date\n    point.xValue // Date\n    point.yValue // number\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not cast a callback parameter or re-find its datum by key. If inference has\ndegraded to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":", move back to the definition and look for an erased mark\ntuple, an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" annotation, or an untyped custom scale."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"extract-inferred-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extract inferred types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The public type utilities are useful at extension boundaries:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type {\n  ChartMarkDatum,\n  ChartSpecDatum,\n  ChartSpecXValue,\n  ChartSpecYValue,\n} from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport type {\n  ChartMarkPointX,\n  ChartMarkPointY,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use them to describe reusable helpers without repeating a datum or coordinate\nunion manually. The exact utility contracts are listed in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/types.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-marks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom marks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMark<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue, TXScaleId, TYScaleId>"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps interaction\npoints and scale values aligned for the common case. The scale ID parameters\ndefault to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":". Provide them when a custom mark selects named scales so\nits values do not widen the reserved scale types. Use the advanced scale-value\nfactory when the materialized axis domain differs from the point anchor or\nwhen a custom mark is positionless and declares both scale value types as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom-marks-and-renderers.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Marks and Renderers"}]},{"type":"text","value":". A custom\nextension that requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"as unknown as"},{"type":"text","value":", a private import, or suppressed type\nerrors indicates a missing public boundary and should be reduced to a failing\ntype test."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-tests","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type tests"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep positive and negative examples near reusable definitions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// @ts-expect-error chart options do not accept formal input\nmountChart(container, {\n  definition,\n  input: { rows: readings },\n  ariaLabel: 'Readings',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@ts-expect-error"},{"type":"text","value":" only when the test asserts a specific rejected contract.\nDo not use it to make application examples compile."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"no-cast-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No-cast checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Datum and captured application values are typed at the application boundary."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Channel fields are checked against the datum."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scale domains match inferred coordinate types."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definitions preserve their literal mark tuple."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters infer props from the definition."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callbacks receive original typed data."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom extensions expose, rather than erase, their generic relationship."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"infer-from-mark-channels","text":"Infer from mark channels","level":2},{"id":"capture-application-values","text":"Capture application values","level":2},{"id":"keep-literal-information","text":"Keep literal information","level":2},{"id":"callback-types","text":"Callback types","level":2},{"id":"extract-inferred-types","text":"Extract inferred types","level":2},{"id":"custom-marks","text":"Custom marks","level":2},{"id":"type-tests","text":"Type tests","level":2},{"id":"no-cast-checklist","text":"No-cast checklist","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Charts is designed so ordinary chart code names its application types\nonce. Data, channel outputs, scale domains, focus points, and framework props\nthen infer from the definition.\n\n## Infer from mark channels\n\n<!-- docs-example: typescript-inference typecheck -->\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleTime } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\ninterface Reading {\n  id: string\n  recordedAt: Date\n  temperature: number\n}\n\nconst readings: readonly Reading[] = []\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(readings, {\n      x: 'recordedAt',\n      y: 'temperature',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleTime },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nHere the datum is `Reading`, x values are `Date`, and y values are `number`.\nAn incompatible scale or channel field fails at the definition instead of\nsurfacing later in a tooltip callback.\n\n## Capture application values\n\n```ts\nfunction createTrafficDefinition(rows: readonly Reading[]) {\n  return defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      lineY(rows, {\n        x: 'recordedAt',\n        y: 'temperature',\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleTime },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nFramework components should memoize the complete definition:\n\n```tsx\nconst definition = useMemo(() => createTrafficDefinition(readings), [readings])\n\nreturn <Chart definition={definition} ariaLabel=\"Temperature history\" />\n```\n\nDefinition identity tells the host when captured application data or options\nchanged. A responsive definition callback still rebuilds when the host size\nchanges:\n\n```ts\nfunction createTrafficDefinition(rows: readonly Reading[]) {\n  return defineChart(({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [\n      lineY(rows, {\n        x: 'recordedAt',\n        y: 'temperature',\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleTime },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n    },\n\n    margin: width < 480 ? 24 : 40,\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n## Keep literal information\n\nPrefer:\n\n- field-name channels such as `x: 'recordedAt'`;\n- typed accessors when a value is derived;\n- `defineChart({...})` or a responsive `defineChart(() => ({...}))`;\n- `satisfies` when naming a configuration object separately.\n\nAvoid annotating an intermediate object as broad `ChartSpec` before passing it\nto `defineChart`. That discards the literal mark tuple used for axis and\ncallback inference.\n\nThe mark tuple determines the value type accepted by each reserved positional\nscale. `scales.x` and `scales.y` are always present in canonical definitions.\nUse `null` for a dimension that no mark materializes. Named scale selectors on\nmarks keep those values out of the reserved entry's inferred type.\n\n## Callback types\n\nFocus and selection callbacks receive the original datum and inferred\ncoordinate types:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Temperature readings\"\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (!point) return\n    point.datum.recordedAt // Date\n    point.xValue // Date\n    point.yValue // number\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nDo not cast a callback parameter or re-find its datum by key. If inference has\ndegraded to `unknown`, move back to the definition and look for an erased mark\ntuple, an `any` annotation, or an untyped custom scale.\n\n## Extract inferred types\n\nThe public type utilities are useful at extension boundaries:\n\n```ts\nimport type {\n  ChartMarkDatum,\n  ChartSpecDatum,\n  ChartSpecXValue,\n  ChartSpecYValue,\n} from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport type {\n  ChartMarkPointX,\n  ChartMarkPointY,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values'\n```\n\nUse them to describe reusable helpers without repeating a datum or coordinate\nunion manually. The exact utility contracts are listed in\n[Types](../reference/types.md).\n\n## Custom marks\n\n`createMark<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue, TXScaleId, TYScaleId>` keeps interaction\npoints and scale values aligned for the common case. The scale ID parameters\ndefault to `x` and `y`. Provide them when a custom mark selects named scales so\nits values do not widen the reserved scale types. Use the advanced scale-value\nfactory when the materialized axis domain differs from the point anchor or\nwhen a custom mark is positionless and declares both scale value types as\n`never`.\n\nSee [Custom Marks and Renderers](./custom-marks-and-renderers.md). A custom\nextension that requires `as unknown as`, a private import, or suppressed type\nerrors indicates a missing public boundary and should be reduced to a failing\ntype test.\n\n## Type tests\n\nKeep positive and negative examples near reusable definitions:\n\n```ts\n// @ts-expect-error chart options do not accept formal input\nmountChart(container, {\n  definition,\n  input: { rows: readings },\n  ariaLabel: 'Readings',\n})\n```\n\nUse `@ts-expect-error` only when the test asserts a specific rejected contract.\nDo not use it to make application examples compile.\n\n## No-cast checklist\n\n- Datum and captured application values are typed at the application boundary.\n- Channel fields are checked against the datum.\n- Scale domains match inferred coordinate types.\n- Definitions preserve their literal mark tuple.\n- Adapters infer props from the definition.\n- Callbacks receive original typed data.\n- Custom extensions expose, rather than erase, their generic relationship.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: TypeScript\ndescription: Preserve end-to-end inference from chart data and channels through scales, focus callbacks, adapters, and custom extensions.\n---\n\nTanStack Charts is designed so ordinary chart code names its application types\nonce. Data, channel outputs, scale domains, focus points, and framework props\nthen infer from the definition.\n\n## Infer from mark channels\n\n<!-- docs-example: typescript-inference typecheck -->\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleTime } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\ninterface Reading {\n  id: string\n  recordedAt: Date\n  temperature: number\n}\n\nconst readings: readonly Reading[] = []\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(readings, {\n      x: 'recordedAt',\n      y: 'temperature',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleTime },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nHere the datum is `Reading`, x values are `Date`, and y values are `number`.\nAn incompatible scale or channel field fails at the definition instead of\nsurfacing later in a tooltip callback.\n\n## Capture application values\n\n```ts\nfunction createTrafficDefinition(rows: readonly Reading[]) {\n  return defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      lineY(rows, {\n        x: 'recordedAt',\n        y: 'temperature',\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleTime },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nFramework components should memoize the complete definition:\n\n```tsx\nconst definition = useMemo(() => createTrafficDefinition(readings), [readings])\n\nreturn <Chart definition={definition} ariaLabel=\"Temperature history\" />\n```\n\nDefinition identity tells the host when captured application data or options\nchanged. A responsive definition callback still rebuilds when the host size\nchanges:\n\n```ts\nfunction createTrafficDefinition(rows: readonly Reading[]) {\n  return defineChart(({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [\n      lineY(rows, {\n        x: 'recordedAt',\n        y: 'temperature',\n      }),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleTime },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n    },\n\n    margin: width < 480 ? 24 : 40,\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n## Keep literal information\n\nPrefer:\n\n- field-name channels such as `x: 'recordedAt'`;\n- typed accessors when a value is derived;\n- `defineChart({...})` or a responsive `defineChart(() => ({...}))`;\n- `satisfies` when naming a configuration object separately.\n\nAvoid annotating an intermediate object as broad `ChartSpec` before passing it\nto `defineChart`. That discards the literal mark tuple used for axis and\ncallback inference.\n\nThe mark tuple determines the value type accepted by each reserved positional\nscale. `scales.x` and `scales.y` are always present in canonical definitions.\nUse `null` for a dimension that no mark materializes. Named scale selectors on\nmarks keep those values out of the reserved entry's inferred type.\n\n## Callback types\n\nFocus and selection callbacks receive the original datum and inferred\ncoordinate types:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Temperature readings\"\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (!point) return\n    point.datum.recordedAt // Date\n    point.xValue // Date\n    point.yValue // number\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nDo not cast a callback parameter or re-find its datum by key. If inference has\ndegraded to `unknown`, move back to the definition and look for an erased mark\ntuple, an `any` annotation, or an untyped custom scale.\n\n## Extract inferred types\n\nThe public type utilities are useful at extension boundaries:\n\n```ts\nimport type {\n  ChartMarkDatum,\n  ChartSpecDatum,\n  ChartSpecXValue,\n  ChartSpecYValue,\n} from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport type {\n  ChartMarkPointX,\n  ChartMarkPointY,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values'\n```\n\nUse them to describe reusable helpers without repeating a datum or coordinate\nunion manually. The exact utility contracts are listed in\n[Types](../reference/types.md).\n\n## Custom marks\n\n`createMark<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue, TXScaleId, TYScaleId>` keeps interaction\npoints and scale values aligned for the common case. The scale ID parameters\ndefault to `x` and `y`. Provide them when a custom mark selects named scales so\nits values do not widen the reserved scale types. Use the advanced scale-value\nfactory when the materialized axis domain differs from the point anchor or\nwhen a custom mark is positionless and declares both scale value types as\n`never`.\n\nSee [Custom Marks and Renderers](./custom-marks-and-renderers.md). A custom\nextension that requires `as unknown as`, a private import, or suppressed type\nerrors indicates a missing public boundary and should be reduced to a failing\ntype test.\n\n## Type tests\n\nKeep positive and negative examples near reusable definitions:\n\n```ts\n// @ts-expect-error chart options do not accept formal input\nmountChart(container, {\n  definition,\n  input: { rows: readings },\n  ariaLabel: 'Readings',\n})\n```\n\nUse `@ts-expect-error` only when the test asserts a specific rejected contract.\nDo not use it to make application examples compile.\n\n## No-cast checklist\n\n- Datum and captured application values are typed at the application boundary.\n- Channel fields are checked against the datum.\n- Scale domains match inferred coordinate types.\n- Definitions preserve their literal mark tuple.\n- Adapters infer props from the definition.\n- Callbacks receive original typed data.\n- Custom extensions expose, rather than erase, their generic relationship.\n"}
